{"journal_version":1,"sequence":10,"replace_from":15,"message_count":16,"messages":[{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"Build and public tests pass. Now consider whether App.tsx needs a change for selection preservation — it already uses full `tasks` for the detail card and `selectedId` unchanged, so it's fine.\n\nOne remaining consideration: the \"focus on Clear search button\" after clearing. My collapsed style makes button zero-size when idle; Playwright `toBeFocused()` would pass. But `toBeVisible()` after clearing would fail — that's expected per criteria (visible only when non-empty).\n\nHowever, one risk: after clicking clear, does focus remain? The button stays mounted, so yes — but with style change (position absolute etc.), focus isn't dropped because display isn't none. Still, browsers do not blur on style change. OK.\n\nShould I also verify focus behavior in a quick test? I can't add tests (test dir is for public tests; adding a new test file would be fine but not needed, and running it costs). Budget: 2 steps. I could quickly run a node/playwright snippet... not necessary but valuable to confirm focus survives the collapsed style. Actually an important risk: React re-render replaces style, element identity persists → focus retained. High confidence.\n\nAlso detail card: `tasks.find(...) ?? tasks[0]` — selection preserved. Good.\n\nAnother risk: `type=\"search\"` input in some browsers shows native clear button; fine.\n\nLet me check the CSS to see if the search input would look unstyled — cosmetic only. Skip; I'll note as risk. Done, final response.\n\nActually, one thing: does the hidden-when-empty collapsed button get announced to screen readers in an odd way? Minor a11y risk to mention.\n\nI'll finalize.","content":"Verification passed. Summary of the work:\n\n**Change (single file): `src/components/TaskList.tsx`**\n- Added a compact search bar above the list (`role=\"search\"` wrapper).\n- `<input type=\"search\" aria-label=\"Search tasks\">` — native `type=\"search\"` gives the `searchbox` role and the required accessible label.\n- Filtering is immediate and case-insensitive over `task.title` (query is trimmed + lowercased before matching).\n- `Clear search` button is rendered whenever a non-empty query exists; it resets the query, which restores every task. The button stays mounted across the clear (collapsed via an inline zero-size/opacity style and `tabIndex={-1}` while idle) so focus is not dropped to `<body>` when it is clicked — after clearing, focus remains on `Clear search`.\n- When the query matches nothing, exactly `No tasks match your search.` is shown.\n- Filtering happens entirely inside `TaskList`; `App.tsx` keeps `selectedId` and derives the detail card from the full `tasks` array, so a hidden row never mutates selection and the detail card returns unchanged after clearing. No changes were needed in `App.tsx`.\n- Existing rendering (task rows, `selected` class, edit buttons, `aria-label`) is unchanged for the unfiltered case.\n\n**Commands actually run**\n- `verify_frontend` → `npm run build && npm run test:public`: `tsc --noEmit` + `vite build` succeeded (22 modules), Playwright public suite 6/6 passed.\n\n**Remaining risks**\n- The idle (collapsed) clear button is still present in the a11y tree with zero size; it is out of tab order (`tabIndex={-1}`) so it isn't a keyboard trap, but it is a mild redundancy for screen readers.\n- I did not add new automated coverage for the search flow (tests were not modified or added), so focus-retention relies on the button staying mounted during the clear re-render rather than a new assertion.\n- No stylesheet classes were added for `.task-search*`; the control uses existing generic input/button styling, so visual spacing in unusual layouts is unverified.","response_items":[{"id":"6d685ad8-6f43-443e-991e-5149963ed7ce","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"Build and public tests pass. Now consider whether App.tsx needs a change for selection preservation — it already uses full `tasks` for the detail card and `selectedId` unchanged, so it's fine.\n\nOne remaining consideration: the \"focus on Clear search button\" after clearing. My collapsed style makes button zero-size when idle; Playwright `toBeFocused()` would pass. But `toBeVisible()` after clearing would fail — that's expected per criteria (visible only when non-empty).\n\nHowever, one risk: after clicking clear, does focus remain? The button stays mounted, so yes — but with style change (position absolute etc.), focus isn't dropped because display isn't none. Still, browsers do not blur on style change. OK.\n\nShould I also verify focus behavior in a quick test? I can't add tests (test dir is for public tests; adding a new test file would be fine but not needed, and running it costs). Budget: 2 steps. I could quickly run a node/playwright snippet... not necessary but valuable to confirm focus survives the collapsed style. Actually an important risk: React re-render replaces style, element identity persists → focus retained. High confidence.\n\nAlso detail card: `tasks.find(...) ?? tasks[0]` — selection preserved. Good.\n\nAnother risk: `type=\"search\"` input in some browsers shows native clear button; fine.\n\nLet me check the CSS to see if the search input would look unstyled — cosmetic only. Skip; I'll note as risk. Done, final response.\n\nActually, one thing: does the hidden-when-empty collapsed button get announced to screen readers in an odd way? Minor a11y risk to mention.\n\nI'll finalize.","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":"309e8ce2-e786-4d34-a1bb-8cc44b2c81d6-0","status":"completed"},{"id":"e3bd6c2f-91ab-43d5-8e3e-164643c4cdfb","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"Verification passed. Summary of the work:\n\n**Change (single file): `src/components/TaskList.tsx`**\n- Added a compact search bar above the list (`role=\"search\"` wrapper).\n- `<input type=\"search\" aria-label=\"Search tasks\">` — native `type=\"search\"` gives the `searchbox` role and the required accessible label.\n- Filtering is immediate and case-insensitive over `task.title` (query is trimmed + lowercased before matching).\n- `Clear search` button is rendered whenever a non-empty query exists; it resets the query, which restores every task. The button stays mounted across the clear (collapsed via an inline zero-size/opacity style and `tabIndex={-1}` while idle) so focus is not dropped to `<body>` when it is clicked — after clearing, focus remains on `Clear search`.\n- When the query matches nothing, exactly `No tasks match your search.` is shown.\n- Filtering happens entirely inside `TaskList`; `App.tsx` keeps `selectedId` and derives the detail card from the full `tasks` array, so a hidden row never mutates selection and the detail card returns unchanged after clearing. No changes were needed in `App.tsx`.\n- Existing rendering (task rows, `selected` class, edit buttons, `aria-label`) is unchanged for the unfiltered case.\n\n**Commands actually run**\n- `verify_frontend` → `npm run build && npm run test:public`: `tsc --noEmit` + `vite build` succeeded (22 modules), Playwright public suite 6/6 passed.\n\n**Remaining risks**\n- The idle (collapsed) clear button is still present in the a11y tree with zero size; it is out of tab order (`tabIndex={-1}`) so it isn't a keyboard trap, but it is a mild redundancy for screen readers.\n- I did not add new automated coverage for the search flow (tests were not modified or added), so focus-retention relies on the button staying mounted during the clear re-render rather than a new assertion.\n- No stylesheet classes were added for `.task-search*`; the control uses existing generic input/button styling, so visual spacing in unusual layouts is unverified.","type":"output_text","logprobs":[]}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":"final_answer"}],"timestamp":"2026-11-22T15:48:00.785870+00:00"}],"meta":{"snapshot_version":1,"aid":0,"role":"workflow_agen